# Project Engineering Rules

This repository follows [Eric's Engineering Constitution](constitution/CONSTITUTION.md).

## Required Workflow

1. Read `constitution/CONSTITUTION.md` and `constitution/AI_WORKFLOW.md`.
2. Check `docs/SESSION_PLAN.md` for a previous interrupted session; write your own plan before implementing.
3. Read `docs/MEMORY.md` to load project context, codebase learnings, and user preferences.
4. Follow the project conventions in `AGENTS.md`.
5. Update tests, docs, `TODO.md`, and `CHANGELOG.md` as part of every change.
6. Propose new codebase learnings, user preferences, or major decisions to the user and (upon approval) record them in `docs/MEMORY.md` before completing work.
7. Keep the demo page current — when a change alters user-facing behavior and the repository has a `demo.html`, update it in the same change; a demo still showing the old behavior is an incomplete change (`constitution/DOCUMENTATION.md`, "Demo Page").
8. Consult and extend the session log — before planning, read the newest rows of `docs/sessions/README.md` and search `docs/sessions/` for earlier sessions on the same topic (`bash constitution/scripts/find_sessions.sh <keyword>`), reading the ones that match; before completing non-trivial work, add this session's summary there (request, context, decisions, discoveries, outcome — a summary, never a transcript, and never a secret) and list it in the index (`constitution/AI_WORKFLOW.md`, "Session Summaries").
